# starling-quantize recipe: the phone-sized Parakeet TDT v3 (364 MB, -34 % vs
# the q4_k_m-shrink16 file the app downloads today). Every linear Q4_0 —
# including the conformer pointwise convs, which every earlier recipe kept at
# F16 (151 MB, 27 % of the q4_k_m file) and which are opt-in here; the
# quantizer writes them flattened [in, out] — with the duration-sensitive
# 640-wide joint/LSTM and the prediction embedding at Q8_0 (making those
# Q4_0 too cost +0.4 pt German WER).
#
# Why Q4_0: on arm64 it repacks into the i8mm 4x8 GEMM, and the phone's Vulkan
# fast engine maps Q4_0/Q8_0 onto its W4/W8 layouts losslessly (Q4_K/Q6_K are
# re-rounded there).
#
# Measured (2026-10-11, F32 source, parakeet-full.imx; FLEURS test, 100 clips
# per language, paired bootstrap vs F32): en 5.33 % vs 5.61 % (clip delta
# -0.31 pt [-0.80, +0.13]), de 4.46 % vs 4.68 % (-0.20 pt [-0.60, +0.19]).
# Pixel 10 Pro vs q4_k_m-shrink16 (benchmarks/quant_phone/phone_quant_bench.sh,
# on battery, ABBA rounds, medians): Vulkan fast engine (the app's default)
# load 1.88 vs 2.30 s, medium 2.06 vs 2.26 s, long 6.91 vs 7.69 s, peak RSS
# 778 vs 1180 MB, ~-15 % energy per process (coulomb counter), fixture
# transcripts identical; ggml CPU peak RSS 548 vs 728 MB, CPU time -10 %.
# Notebook RADV: transcripts identical, latency within 8 %.
#
#   build/starling-quantize \
#       --input models/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-f32.gguf \
#       --output models/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-q4pw-fullimx.gguf \
#       --recipe quants/recipes/parakeet-q4pw-fullimx.recipe \
#       --imatrix models/parakeet-full.imx --shrink-f16
default q4_0
^encoder\.layers\.[0-9]+\.conv\.pointwise_conv[12]\.weight$ q4_0
^decoder\.prediction\.embed\.weight$ q8_0
^joint\. q8_0
^decoder\.prediction\.dec_rnn\. q8_0
